  /* ================= FULL SCREEN =================
     Measured on the reference: a near-opaque dark field (rgba(20,22,24,.95))
     with the picture centred on it. `contain` here, not `cover`: this view
     exists to show the whole photograph, which is the opposite of the crop the
     wall may apply. */
  .full {
    position: fixed;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 200;
    display: grid;
    /* WARNING: `1fr` IS `minmax(auto, 1fr)`, AND `auto` IS THE CONTENT'S OWN
       SIZE - the grid track grows to the picture and `max-height: 100%` then
       measures against that oversized track. Measured with a portrait file:
       the image came out 1344x1792 inside a 900px viewport, i.e. the layer
       scrolled. `minmax(0, …)` is the grid equivalent of the `flex-basis: 0`
       trap in §5.189. */
    grid-template-rows: minmax(0, 1fr);
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    place-items: center;
    padding: clamp(1rem, 4vw, 3rem);
